 "ship_line_caveat": "the ship rule (F1 >= 0.70 out-of-fold) was fixed before these numbers were seen and is applied as stated. But at n=400 the per-class CIs are wide: four of seven classes have a 95% CI straddling 0.70, so for those the ship/withhold call is not resolvable on this sample. Only SW and SALES sit entirely above the line and only MGT entirely below. HEALTH ships on a point estimate of 0.741 whose interval reaches 0.588 -- treat it as provisional, not as a measured pass.",
